# Line endings.
#
# Several files in this repo are under a content freeze: `evals/analysis/*/freeze.json`
# records a SHA-256 per file and `verify_fixture_freeze` / `verify_standards_freeze`
# refuse to run if any of them changed. Those hashes were taken over LF bytes.
#
# On Windows, `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites text files to CRLF on checkout. The
# committed bytes are unchanged and `git status` stays clean, but the working-tree
# bytes no longer hash to the frozen value, so every frozen file reports as drifted
# at once. Pinning these types to LF keeps the checked-out bytes equal to the
# committed bytes on every platform.
#
# The frozen material is JSON (fixtures), Python (criterion tests) and Markdown
# (methodology), so all three are pinned. The index is already LF throughout, so
# this changes what checkout writes and nothing else.

*.json  text eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
